Keep personal-assistant tools when the Terminus heuristic misfires.

Upstream https://github.com/odysseus-dev/odysseus/issues/6194 (open).

_LOCAL_COMPUTER_REFERENCE_RE treats any "on/from <word>" as a machine
name -- "summarize my emails from today" matches on "from today" -- and
the clamp then REPLACES the retrieved tool set with the shell/file
Terminus toolset, so the agent truthfully reports it has no email tools.
Bail out when intent detection confidently fired a personal-assistant
domain, the same way the clamp already defers to an active document.

--- a/src/agent_loop.py
+++ b/src/agent_loop.py
@@ -3977,6 +3977,10 @@
             )
             and not _active_document_relevant
             and not active_email
+            # "from today" / "from gmail" in a mail request is not a hostname:
+            # a confidently-detected personal-assistant domain must never be
+            # clamped away to the shell/file toolset. Upstream #6194.
+            and not ({"email", "notes_calendar_tasks", "documents"} & set(_intent.get("domains") or []))
         ):
             _relevant_tools = set(_WORKSPACE_TERMINUS_TOOLS)
             logger.info("[tool-rag] Workspace file/terminal request; using Odysseus Terminus toolset")
